 (exe name)←EstablishComparisonTool default;qdmx
⍝ Establishes the comparison utility that is going to be used for comparing two files.\\
⍝ `default` is the name of a preferred utility; it may well be empty. Typically this is
⍝ what the user specified via the `-use=` modifier.\\
⍝ Returns the name of the executable together with the name of the utility, or two empty
⍝ vectors in case the user command `CompareFiles` is not available, the user cancelled the
⍝ selection, or `CompareFiles` did not cooperate. Therefore a caller **must** check `exe`
⍝ rather than assuming that a comparison utility is available.
 (exe name)←'' ''
 :If 9=⎕SE.⎕NC'CompareFiles'
     :Trap 911
         (exe name)←⎕SE.CompareFiles.EstablishCompareEXE default
     :Else
         qdmx←⎕DMX
         ⎕←'Comparison with "CompareFiles" crashed'{0=≢⍵:⍺ ⋄ ⍺,' with "',⍵,'"'}qdmx.EM
         (exe name)←'' ''
     :EndTrap
 :EndIf
⍝Done
